    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "The deck is shuffled and dealt out equally to players face-down; players do not look at their cards. Player to dealer's left begins; turn passes clockwise. On your turn you turn the top card of your face-down pile and place it face-up alongside, forming a face-up pile beside your face-down pile. When two face-up pile tops match in rank (e.g. two sixes), any player who notices may shout Snap; the first to do so takes both matching face-up piles and adds them face-down to the bottom of their face-down pile. Play continues from the player to the left of whoever turned. If you have no face-down cards when it is your turn, turn your face-up pile over to make a new face-down pile and turn the top card. If you have no cards at all you are out. Last player with cards wins. If a player shouts Snap in error, that player's face-up pile is put in the centre as a snap pool; if the top of any pile later matches the top of a snap pool, the first to call Snap pool takes both piles.",
    Player: "The deck is shuffled and dealt out equally to players face-down; players do not look at their cards. Player to dealer's left begins; turn passes clockwise. On your turn you turn the top card of your face-down pile and place it face-up alongside, forming a face-up pile beside your face-down pile. When two face-up pile tops match in rank (e.g. two sixes), any player who notices may shout Snap; the first to do so takes both matching face-up piles and adds them face-down to the bottom of their face-down pile. Play continues from the player to the left of whoever turned. If you have no face-down cards when it is your turn, turn your face-up pile over to make a new face-down pile and turn the top card. If you have no cards at all you are out. Last player with cards wins. If a player shouts Snap in error, that player's face-up pile is put in the centre as a snap pool; if the top of any pile later matches the top of a snap pool, the first to call Snap pool takes both piles.",
    objective: 'Be the last player with cards by calling Snap when two face-up pile tops match in rank; the first to call wins those piles and adds them to the bottom of their face-down pile.',
    gameplay: "The deck is shuffled and dealt out equally to players face-down; players do not look at their cards. Player to dealer's left begins; turn passes clockwise. On your turn you turn the top card of your face-down pile and place it face-up alongside, forming a face-up pile beside your face-down pile. When two face-up pile tops match in rank (e.g. two sixes), any player who notices may shout Snap; the first to do so takes both matching face-up piles and adds them face-down to the bottom of their face-down pile. Play continues from the player to the left of whoever turned. If you have no face-down cards when it is your turn, turn your face-up pile over to make a new face-down pile and turn the top card. If you have no cards at all you are out. Last player with cards wins. If a player shouts Snap in error, that player's face-up pile is put in the centre as a snap pool; if the top of any pile later matches the top of a snap pool, the first to call Snap pool takes both piles.",
    keyRules: [
      'Deal entire deck equally face-down; players do not look at cards.',
      'Turn top card face-up on your turn; turn the card facing away from yourself so others see it first.',
      'When two face-up pile tops match in rank, any player may shout Snap; first to do so wins both piles.',
      'False snap: your face-up pile is moved to the centre as a snap pool.',
      'When a pile top matches a snap pool top, first to call Snap pool wins both.',
      'No face-down cards on your turn: turn your face-up pile over and continue; no cards at all means you are out.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
